{
  "work_package_id": "WP-009",
  "work_package_file": "work/WP-009.md",
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS",
  "assigned_to": "QA",
  "dependencies": [
    "WP-006"
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "criterion": "normaliseRepo() maps CredentialId to credentialId in the normalised repository object.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The repository detail view (#/repositories/:id) shows a \"Credential\" section with a <select> dropdown.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The dropdown is populated from GET /api/repositories/:id/credential-options with options: \"None\" + each matching credential displayed as label (host).",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "When exactly one credential matches (auto-selected), it is pre-selected in the dropdown with an \"(auto)\" indicator.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "When a stored CredentialId exists, the corresponding credential is pre-selected in the dropdown.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "Changing the dropdown selection calls PUT /api/repositories/:id/credential to persist the choice.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The repository list view table shows a credential status indicator for each repository row.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The project-detail view's buildRepositoriesSection() repository table shows the same credential status indicator.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "api.repositories.updateCredential(id, credentialId) sends PUT /api/repositories/:id/credential with the correct body.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "api.repositories.credentialOptions(id) sends GET /api/repositories/:id/credential-options.",
      "met": true
    },
    {
      "criterion": "All GUI tests for normalise.test.mjs, repository-detail.test.mjs, repositories.test.mjs, and api.config.test.mjs pass.",
      "met": true
    }
  ],
  "active_pipeline_stages": [
    "implementation",
    "qa",
    "code-review",
    "documentation"
  ],
  "revision": 0,
  "pipelines": [
    {
      "type": "implementation",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-26T13:36:43Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-06-26T13:43:27Z",
      "duration_ms": 404000,
      "summary": [
        "Implemented all GUI credential selector and status indicator features for WP-009.",
        "normaliseRepo() updated to map CredentialId → credentialId following the existing Go-capitalised → camelCase pattern.",
        "api.repositories.credentialOptions(id) added: sends GET /api/repositories/:id/credential-options.",
        "api.repositories.updateCredential(id, credentialId) added: sends PUT /api/repositories/:id/credential with { credentialId } body.",
        "repositories.js list view: added 'Credential' column header and per-row credential status badge (🔑 when set, — when none), using CSS classes credential-status-badge--set / credential-status-badge--none.",
        "project-detail.js buildRepositoriesSection(): added 'Credential' column header and same credential status badge per row using the normalised credentialId field.",
        "repository-detail.js: added buildCredentialSection(repoId, storedCredentialId) which asynchronously fetches credential-options, renders a <select> with 'None' + each credential as 'label (host)', handles auto-selection (single auto-match pre-selected with '(auto)' indicator), handles stored credentialId pre-selection, and persists changes via updateCredential on change events.",
        "Credential section is mounted between the header and the workspace status table in renderRepositoryDetail.",
        "All tests pass: normalise.test.mjs (22), api.config.test.mjs (30), repositories.test.mjs (9), repository-detail.test.mjs (29)."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "gui/public/js/utils/normalise.js",
          "gui/public/js/api.js",
          "gui/public/js/views/repositories.js",
          "gui/public/js/views/project-detail.js",
          "gui/public/js/views/repository-detail.js",
          "gui/public/js/__tests__/normalise.test.mjs",
          "gui/public/js/api.config.test.mjs",
          "gui/public/js/views/repositories.test.mjs",
          "gui/public/js/views/repository-detail.test.mjs"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T13:43:27Z",
          "note": "repository-detail.js buildCredentialSection() uses a fire-and-forget async IIFE pattern (calling api.repositories.credentialOptions inside .then chains attached to a synchronously-returned section element). This is consistent with the existing loadWorkspaceRows pattern in the same file, but a future refactor could use an async helper that returns the section after the fetch resolves, reducing the need for internal DOM mutation post-render."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T13:43:27Z",
          "note": "The credential status badge in repositories.js and project-detail.js uses an emoji (🔑) as the 'set' indicator. While visually clear, emoji rendering can vary across platforms and screen readers. A CSS-based icon or text badge (e.g. 'Set') with a consistent aria-label would be more accessible and easier to style."
        },
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T13:43:27Z",
          "note": "normalise.js has no tests for normaliseRepo() for its core fields (id, name, url, LastRefreshedAt) — only the new CredentialId mapping is tested. The existing AC tests for the views implicitly exercise normaliseRepo() but dedicated unit tests for all fields would improve isolation. Out of scope for this WP but worth noting."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-26T13:43:49Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-06-26T13:50:09Z",
      "duration_ms": 380000,
      "summary": [
        "All 11 acceptance criteria verified — build clean, all 90 WP-009 tests pass (normalise: 22, api.config: 30, repositories: 9, repository-detail: 29). Full regression suite also passes (settings: 17, workspace-detail: 26, repo-status-cells/dashboard/api-misc: 59). All AC confirmed via direct source inspection and live Node.js edge-case execution."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "test_coverage": "100% of WP-009 AC covered by automated tests",
        "tests_passed": 90,
        "tests_failed": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T13:50:09Z",
          "note": "api.repositories.updateCredential(id, credentialId) uses JSON.stringify({ credentialId }) — if called with undefined (not in the current UI code path), JSON.stringify silently strips the key, producing {} body instead of { credentialId: '' }. Not a real bug (UI always passes a string from select.value), but defensive input validation (throw if credentialId is not a string) would harden the contract."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T13:50:09Z",
          "note": "The auto-select logic (line 116 of repository-detail.js) requires exactly one option AND auto=true. If the backend returns multiple options all with auto=true (e.g. multiple credentials for the same host), none would be auto-selected. This is likely intentional but the divergence between backend semantics and this guard is worth documenting in the JSDoc."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T13:50:09Z",
          "note": "The credential status badge in repositories.js and project-detail.js uses emoji 🔑 as the visual indicator. The aria-label ('Credential configured') provides screen-reader accessibility, but emoji rendering may vary cross-platform. A CSS icon or text label ('Set') would be more consistent — flagging this per Developer handoff note."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "status_changed_at": "2026-06-26T13:36:43Z",
  "last_updated": "2026-06-26T13:50:09Z",
  "handoff_notes": [
    {
      "from_agent": "Developer",
      "to_agent": "QA",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-26T13:43:27Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 11 acceptance criteria are met and all tests pass (normalise.test.mjs: 22 pass, api.config.test.mjs: 30 pass, repositories.test.mjs: 9 pass, repository-detail.test.mjs: 29 pass).",
        "The credential selector section in repository-detail.js uses an async fetch on mount — QA should verify the dropdown renders correctly after a short delay (two setTimeout(0) flushes in tests cover this).",
        "The credential status badge uses emoji 🔑 for 'set' and — for 'none' — these are intentional placeholders that the QA and reviewer agents may flag for accessibility improvement (noted as code insight observation)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-26T13:50:09Z",
      "notes": [
        "All 11 ACs confirmed PASS via test execution and source inspection. No regressions in 199 total tests across the GUI. Two low-priority improvement observations noted: (1) updateCredential(id, undefined) sends empty body — document that callers must pass '' to clear; (2) auto-select logic requires exactly one option with auto=true — worth adding JSDoc note. Emoji badge accessibility is a pre-existing low-priority item. No blocking issues for code review."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

